Reason:
The function calls skb_pull() without first calling pskb_may_pull() to ensure that the data at skb_gro_offset is in the linear area. When skb_headlen is 0 (e.g., from napi_gro_frags), skb_pull decrements skb->len but not skb->data_len, triggering BUG_ON(skb->len < skb->data_len) in __skb_pull().

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (!pskb_may_pull(skb, skb_gro_offset(skb))) {
