    return -ENOMEM;
}
Reason:
The added pskb_may_pull() guard ensures the data is in the linear area before calling skb_pull(). On failure, the skb is flushed (not aggregated) and returned with -ENOMEM, preventing the BUG_ON and matching the UDP fraglist GRO handling.

